      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thoughts on this change?\n\nOn l.4050 in this patch, an IllegalStateException is thrown if the same mBinder is registered across network requests therefore with that change, the NoSuchElement exception should no longer occur since it will be superseded by the IllegalStateException (at least should be for this bug if our thinking is correct).\n\nI\u0027m guessing this was added due to an overabundance of caution? If so, I would suggest reconsidering for two reasons:\n- It muddies this CL a bit (at least IMO).\n- More importantly, it\u0027ll hide the error if for whatever reason, the change you added with the IllegalStateException does not get thrown. In that scenario, we\u0027d lose visibility into the error at this layer and it could manifest itself in other places where it could be even more difficult to diagnose.",
      "range": {
